# Delhivery keys and tracking

Carrier keys live on `pickup_locations.delhiveryApiKey`, not env (env has `DELHIVERY_BASE_URL` + webhook secret only).

`getDelhiveryApiKey(pickupLocation, clientId?)` **must** receive a real tenant `clientId` (UUID string). If omitted it `findFirst`s across tenants. Never `parseInt(order.clientId)` — that is `NaN` and drops the filter.

Always pass `clientId` into `delhiveryService.createOrder` / edit / track. Do not log raw API keys.

**Tracking:** match Delhivery results by `tracking_id` / AWB, never by array index. `refresh-statuses` currently zips positionally and reindexes from 0 each batch — do not copy that. Filter `orders` by `clientId` before refresh.

Waybill purchase then DB insert is not transactional today. Prefer: persist the order (or a pending row) and compensate/`cancel` if the carrier call or insert fails. Do not leave live Delhivery waybills with no `orders` row.

DTDC is slip-pool management only (`/api/dtdc-slips`) — there is no DTDC HTTP API.
